<body>
  <%- include('./partials/nav') %>
  <main class="container-fluid p-3 info-container">
    <div class="intro">
      <h1 class="text-center">Get everyone to the table</h1>
      <p>A browser-based virtual tabletop for D&amp;D and other tabletop RPGs. Bring your maps and tokens, draw on the scene, and roll dice together.</p>
      <p>Players can join a simple table by link without creating an account.</p>
      <div class="seo-cta-block"><a class="seo-cta-primary" href="/vtt/guest/start">Try the tabletop</a> <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/vtt-guide">Read the VTT guide</a>
        <p><small>No account needed to try the sandbox.</small></p>
      </div><hr>
    </div>
    <section id="core-features">
      <h2>Prepare the scene</h2>
      <p>Upload a map, add tokens, and adjust the grid to fit your encounter. Keep terrain, objects, and fog on separate layers so you can manage the scene as play unfolds.</p>
      <p>Bring your own artwork or start with the free token pack. Organize reusable maps and tokens into folders for your next session.</p>
      <figure class="toolshot-card">
        <img src="/assets/screen_shots/vtt-screenshot.png" alt="Virtual tabletop with a battle map, tokens, drawing, and table controls." loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Prepare your map, tokens, and grid before the group arrives.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section id="gm-control">
      <h2>Respond to whatever your players do</h2>
      <p>Draw a spell area, mark a blocked passage, or sketch the bridge you hadn’t planned on needing.</p>
      <p>Move, resize, and rotate tokens. Hide pieces until they matter, and lock objects that should stay in place. Keep table chat and dice rolls beside the map.</p>
      <figure class="toolshot-card">
        <img src="/assets/screen_shots/vtt_secret_tunnel.png" alt="Cave encounter with player tokens and map markings." loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Reveal the scene as your players explore.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section id="linked-maps">
      <h2>Move from room to region</h2>
      <p>Use location pins to mark places that matter and portals to move between linked maps.</p>
      <p>Connect encounters across a dungeon, town, or wider world so the next scene is close at hand.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="fast-setup">
      <h2>Start with a link</h2>
      <p>For a simple table, send your players the join link. They can enter without signing up.</p>
      <p>Want to get familiar with the controls first? Open the no-signup sandbox and try them yourself.</p>
      <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/vtt/guest/start">Try the sandbox</a>
    </section>
    <section id="campaign-depth">
      <h2>Keep the campaign together</h2>
      <p>For an ongoing game, connect your tables through a Wyrld. Keep campaign notes, shared assets, calendars, and linked character sheets with the group that uses them.</p>
      <p>Wyrld members create accounts so they can return to the same shared campaign space.</p>
      <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/wyrlds">Explore Wyrlds</a>
    </section>
    <section id="pro-tools">
      <h2>More tools for recurring games</h2>
      <p>Pro adds reusable table templates and installable community Library Packs, helping you bring familiar setups and collections into future sessions.</p>
      <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/pricing">See plans</a>
    </section>
    <section id="alternatives">
      <h2>Is this the tabletop for your group?</h2>
      <p>Far Reach Co. is built for groups that want maps, tokens, drawing, and dice while leaving plenty of room for description and imagination.</p>
      <p>Its focus is hands-on tabletop play. If detailed automation and elaborate lighting simulations are central to your game, consider that when choosing your VTT.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="get-started">
      <h2>Bring your next encounter to life</h2>
      <div class="seo-cta-block"><a class="seo-cta-primary" href="/vtt/guest/start">Try the tabletop</a> <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/register">Create a free account</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <%- include('./partials/footer') %>
</body>

</html>
